Hello Alexander Gal,

Thank you for contacting Trend Micro about the IP being listed on the QIL.

Frequently Asked Questions regarding the QIL:
---------------------------------
[1] The QIL is blocking my mail!
---------------------------------
A. The QIL does not block any mail, mail servers that are subscribed to the QIL should send a temporary failure error to the sending mail server, if it is listed. The sending mail server will attempt to re-deliver the message at a later time and, if it has been removed from the QIL by then, it will be allowed to deliver the email.

-------------------------------------
[2.] Why is my IP address on the QIL?
-------------------------------------
A. IP addresses are listed in the QIL because they were recently involved in sending spam.

------------------------------------------------
[3.] How do I remove my IP address from the QIL?
------------------------------------------------
A. To remove from the QIL, perform a lookup on the IP with the ERS Lookup Tool https://servicecentral.trendmicro.com/en-US/ers. When the lookup is completed click on the 'Remove' link and this IP will be removed immediately. Removal can be requested once per 24 hours.

-----------------------------------------------------------
[4.] Why does my IP address keep getting listed on the QIL?
-----------------------------------------------------------
A. If we have more spam emails submitted to us from an IP address after it was removed from the QIL, your IP may be re-listed.
 This means that whatever issue that caused it to be listed has not been resolved, or another problem is causing spam to originate from this IP address.
 You need to secure the mail server and ensure that it will not be used in the delivery of spam in the future before requesting removal from the QIL.

